    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0754" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–1049</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mao Tse-tung to the
                        Appointed Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yenan</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-12-16">16 December, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear General Hurley</hi>: Thank you very much for
                    your kind letter.<anchor n="98" xml:id="d535-f1"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0755" n="741" xml:id="pg741"/>
                <p>Last November when President Roosevelt was reelected, I sent him a note of
                    congratulations. In his reply,<anchor n="99" xml:id="d535-f2"/> he said that for
                    the defeat of Japanese aggression, he was willing to cooperate with all
                    anti-Japanese forces in China. Please tell your President that I subscribe fully
                    to his policy and that I thank him.</p>
                <p>This letter is transmitted to you through the kindness of Colonel Barrett whom we
                    hope will soon return to Yenan.</p>
                <p>Several other points which I would like to take up with you have been covered by
                    General Chou En-lai in his letter.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d535-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>With best wishes,</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mao Tse Tung</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
